<HelpTab>
    <FluentText>
        <a href="/manage/companies-locations">Companies &amp; Locations</a> is for Admins only.
    </FluentText>

    <HelpSection Title="Company settings">
        <ul>
            <li><strong>Company name</strong>, <strong>Theme color</strong> and a logo, shown in the menu when people
                are signed in.</li>
            <li>An optional login background image.</li>
            <li><strong>Seasonal themes</strong>: decorations in the staff app. <strong>Automatic (follow the
                calendar)</strong> shows falling snow and snow-topped cards from 1 to 26 December, and
                jack-o'-lanterns from 24 to 31 October (UK time). <strong>Off</strong> turns them off for everyone.
                <strong>Christmas (always on)</strong> and <strong>Halloween (always on)</strong> show that season
                straight away, whatever the date, so you can preview it. Set it back to Automatic afterwards.
                Press <strong>Save Changes</strong> to apply it.</li>
        </ul>
        <HelpNote>
            Seasonal themes never appear on kiosk screens, the clock-in terminal or the login page, and anyone can
            turn them off for themselves under <strong>Seasonal Themes</strong> on their account page. With
            reduced motion switched on in the device's settings, the snow stays on the cards but doesn't fall.
        </HelpNote>
    </HelpSection>

    <HelpSection Title="Locations">
        <FluentText>
            Each venue is a location. People sign in to one location at a time, and most management pages work
            on the location you signed in to. Add a location with <strong>New location name</strong>, set its
            <strong>Opening hours</strong>, or deactivate one you no longer use.
        </FluentText>
    </HelpSection>

    <HelpSection Title="Features">
        <FluentText>
            <strong>Features for</strong> your company switches whole modules on or off, such as Training, Staff
            Scheduling, Chat, Onboarding, Announcements and Audio clips. A switch saves as soon as you flip it. Turning a
            feature off hides it from staff (the menu, home screen and dashboards) and blocks its pages, but
            deletes nothing, so turning it back on brings everything back. Admins always see every feature.
        </FluentText>
    </HelpSection>

    <HelpSection Title="Who works where">
        <FluentText>
            <strong>Staff Locations</strong>: choose a person with <strong>Select User</strong> to see their
            <strong>Assigned Locations</strong>, then use <strong>Add Location</strong> or remove one. People can
            only sign in to locations they belong to, and location chat channels follow these memberships.
        </FluentText>
    </HelpSection>
</HelpTab>
